  ],
  "text": "Your body still remembers the exact shape of infections you had as a child. The first line of defence remembers nothing. It attacks anything that looks wrong. That buys time. Behind it, a slower system is taking notes. It builds one antibody shaped to fit one specific invader, and nothing else. That takes days, which is why the first time you meet something, you get ill. Then it keeps a copy. Memory cells holding that shape for decades. Meet it again and the response is so fast you never notice you were infected. Which is the whole trick behind a vaccine. It is not a treatment. It is a training exercise. The shape, without the illness. Your body keeps a wanted list. A vaccine just adds a face to it early. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
